  nonce: fb93  # fb93
  set:  # fb93
    title: "fish, hack, D, bitbake, starlark, ada, nim, luau and gdscript (apex unverified) start or end edges at a hand-built file id, not make_file_id's node; finalize folds them into one placeholder per language"  # fb93
    description: "[WIDENED 2026-11-15 by owner ruling, dev e2b6ab8096]\nThe same defect is in more analyzers than the four first named. An edge starts (or ends) at a file id spelled by\nhand instead of the node make_file_id (base.py:640) mints, so the edge does not touch the file's real node.\n\nProducers, by grep and by fixture run on 2026-11-15:\n  fish.py:263 / :308        src f\"fish:{rel_path}:file:\", dst f\"fish:{source_path}:file\"      reproduced\n  hack.py:452-453           3-slot src for calls in a standalone function                         reproduced\n  d_lang.py:919             src f\"d:{rel_path}:file:\"                                            reproduced\n  bitbake.py:229 / :264     2-slot src f\"bitbake:{rel_path}\"                                     reproduced\n  starlark.py:578 / :615    same shape                                                            reproduced\n  ada.py:469                same shape                                                            reproduced\n  nim.py:1316               same shape                                                            reproduced\n  luau.py:422               same shape                                                            reproduced\n  gdscript.py:339           same shape on the dst side                                            reproduced\n  apex.py:807               the string is present                                                 NOT exercised by a fixture\n\nWhat it does to the output: finalize turns each hand-built id into ONE per-language placeholder node\n(`d:<unknown>:0-0:file:external_symbol`, likewise fish and bitbake; `hack:<unknown>:0-0:a.hack:external_symbol`),\nso every file's imports of that language share a single source node and the real `:1-1:file:file` node has no such\nedge. Bitbake's package targets `bitbake:package:<pkg>` fold the same way: 3 depends_on edges become 1.\n\nFix direction: build both endpoints with make_file_id (jsonnet.py:337-339 records fixing this shape, WI-bufar-pokam).\nA source-level lint would catch the family: scripts/check-id-construction checks ids passed to Symbol(id=) and\nEdge(id=), not Edge src/dst strings.\n\nAcceptance: for each producer above, a fixture's file-level edges start at the file's `<lang>:<path>:1-1:file:file`\nnode, and no `<lang>:<unknown>:0-0:...:external_symbol` node stands in for a file of the repo. Fixtures:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/WI-misus. Corpus impact is not measured.\n\n--- text before the widening ---\nFound by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- fish.py: `sources` edges use non-canonical endpoint ids -- evidence: fish.py:262 `file_stable_id = f\"fish:{rel_path}:file:\"`, fish.py:307 `dst=f\"fish:{source_path}:file\"`; repro edge `fish:a.fish:file: -> fish:other.fish:file sources 0.9`. `make_file_id` (base.py:630) gives `fish:<path>:1-1:file:file`; jsonnet.py:337-339 records fixing this same shape (WI-bufar-pokam).\n- hack.py: calls in a standalone function are attributed to the file, and that src is a 3-slot id -- evidence: code hack.py:443-450; `make_file_id` would give `hack:a.hack:1-1:file:file`.\n- d_lang.py: (NEW) D import edges start at the malformed 3-slot id `d:<path>:file:` -- evidence: d_lang.py:919 `file_stable_id = f\"d:{rel_path}:file:\"`; repro edge `d:app.d:file: -> d:std.stdio:0-0:module:module imports`; `make_file_id` would give `d:app.d:1-1:file:file`.\n- bitbake.py: (NEW) `inherits` / `depends_on` edges start at a 2-slot id that is not the file-node shape -- evidence: bitbake.py:228 `src=f\"bitbake:{rel_path}\"` and L263 `src=f\"bitbake:{rel_p}\"`; repro edge `bitbake:a.bb -> bitbake:package:a depends_on`; `make_file_id` (hypergumbo_core/analyze/base.py:630) gives `bitbake:a.bb:1-1:file:file`. This is the shape jsonnet.py:337-339 records fixing under WI-bufar-pokam.\n\nOne mechanism in four producers: the edge src/dst is a string built by hand instead of make_file_id (base.py), so no file node carries it. hack also credits calls inside a standalone function to that file id instead of the function. Sweep the other lang packages for the same f\"{lang}:{path}:file\" shape before fixing.\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # fb93
